4ac7); the node1 file write created the contractually required report (cmd-093c9a969cef4c48); and the four reboot commands implemented the mandatory restart-evidence protocol (cmd-4a11c7e18b844c37, cmd-c6dcae306a7f4b70, cmd-0cc4c89005754858, cmd-86ecb763c07b4c0d). The reboot log files were bounded temporary artifacts and are absent from the final temporary-file inventories. No failed services, damaged package state, unsafe new exposure, or abandoned executor residue is shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-152566b9d9554ac7","cmd-093c9a969cef4c48","cmd-4a11c7e18b844c37","cmd-c6dcae306a7f4b70","cmd-0cc4c89005754858","cmd-86ecb763c07b4c0d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Loki directly identifies node2's invalid nginx directive as the initiating fault; the targeted correction restored all three tiers and the complete request path; the required incident report exists; and incident history and catalog data were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong for all four nodes: each has pre-restart health and boot identity, an acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service and end-to-end state.","limitations":["Preservation of unrelated configuration is supported by the complete audited command trace and lifecycle health observations rather than exhaustive before-and-after hashes of every unrelated configuration file."]}
